---
description: TypeScript is strict; never use any or silence the compiler
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: true
---

# TypeScript

- Keep `strict` on. Do not add `any`, `as any`, `as unknown as T`, `@ts-ignore`, `@ts-nocheck`, or `@ts-expect-error`.
- Type at the source. Example: `patchCell<K extends keyof BingoCell>(field: K, value: BingoCell[K])`, not `value: any`.
- Prefer `BingoTheme | undefined` and a `BackupPayload` interface over casts.
- Tests: `vi.mocked(useBingoStore)` and objects that satisfy real types. No `(store as any).mockReturnValue`.
- One field, one meaning. Do not keep `title`+`text` or `isCompleted`+`completedAt` as aliases.
- No unused imports, variables, or parameters. `as` only after a runtime check (e.g. FileReader result).
